# A shell script has to reach Linux with LF line endings, whoever checked it out.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows, where git hands out CRLF. docker/run-parity.sh is then
# mounted straight into the container, bash reads `set -euo pipefail\r`, and reports
# "pipefail: invalid option name" - so the local Linux gate died on its first line and every run of
# it since has been checking nothing.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else the container reads as a script.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
